---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Model Registry Guide - CUNY AI Lab" description="Find current CAIL Model API offerings and compare providers, capabilities, context limits, and token prices.">
  <section class="relative pt-24 pb-10 lg:pt-28 lg:pb-12">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-cuny-blue via-cuny-blue to-vibrant-800" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10">
      <a href={`${base}models/`} class="inline-block text-vibrant-200 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-white mb-4">Back to Model Registry</a>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold font-display text-white">How to use the model registry</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-vibrant-200 text-lg max-w-2xl">Find current models and compare the provider offerings available through the CAIL Model API.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="bg-neutral-cream">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 space-y-9 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      <section aria-labelledby="find-heading">
        <h2 id="find-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-neutral-stone mb-3">Find a model</h2>
        <p>Search by model name or API ID, or narrow the list by provider and capability. Filters work together and show the provider offerings that match; choose <strong>Clear filters</strong> to return to the full catalog. The registry includes text and speech offerings, so check the capabilities before choosing a model for your task.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">The catalog loads when you open the page. Choose <strong>Refresh catalog</strong> to check again. If the catalog cannot be loaded, try refreshing; the page clears earlier results so they are not mistaken for current availability.</p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="providers-heading">
        <h2 id="providers-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-neutral-stone mb-3">Compare provider offerings</h2>
        <p>Models are listed by name, with their provider offerings underneath. Each provider has its own API ID, capabilities, context limit, and prices. Different versions stay separate, even when their names are similar.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Context is measured in tokens and can differ by provider. A missing context limit means it has not been published in the catalog. Capabilities describe the current API route; they do not establish model quality or licensing terms.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">A catalog listing does not guarantee that a provider has capacity for every request. The Sandbox has its own model selector, which may offer a smaller selection.</p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="specifications-heading">
        <h2 id="specifications-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-neutral-stone mb-3">Read model specifications</h2>
        <p>Model size is the number of parameters, shown in billions (B). A mixture-of-experts model (MoE) can have a larger total size while using a smaller set of active parameters for each token. Size alone does not measure quality or speed.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Where verified information is available, the model summary links to its source model card and license. <strong>Open weights</strong> means model weights are available to download; consult the linked license for the terms. Missing size or license information is shown as unavailable.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">These reference specifications have their own verification date. The catalog check time covers live provider details. Capability icons accompany text labels in each provider row; the long-context label means that provider reports a context limit of at least 100,000 tokens.</p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="prices-heading">
        <h2 id="prices-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-neutral-stone mb-3">Read token prices</h2>
        <p>Input and output prices are shown in <strong>USD per million tokens</strong>. Input is what you send to the model; output is what it generates. An unpublished price is unknown. A displayed zero means the catalog explicitly reports zero for that token rate.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">OpenRouter prices labeled <strong>from</strong> are the lowest input and output rates among its currently eligible endpoints. Those two rates can come from different endpoints, and the endpoint used for a request can cost more. Additional provider fees are outside the displayed token rates.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">These are provider rates. They do not show your quota balance or the final cost of a request. Prices and availability can change after the displayed check time.</p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="api-heading">
        <h2 id="api-heading" class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-neutral-stone mb-3">Use an API ID</h2>
        <p>Choose <strong>Copy API ID</strong> for the offering you want. Use that exact ID with the appropriate API endpoint for its capabilities. Text generation and speech recognition use different request formats.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">The <a href={`${base}docs/api-keys/`} class="text-vibrant-700 underline underline-offset-2">API key guide</a> explains how to create a personal key and send a chat request. Browsing the registry does not require a key.</p>
      </section>
      <p><a href={`${base}models/`} class="text-vibrant-700 underline underline-offset-2 font-semibold">Browse the model registry</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
